From bed362c6a95e8ec415f5772e05a451c353a1d2ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 14:31:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(app): a touch probe is not judged against the machine's
 spindle range

The machine check compared every tool's catalog rpm with the mounted
machine's spindle window, so a probe's token rpm (1) refused every
probing program on a machine stating a minimum - the Tormach 770MX's
175 rpm among them - though the post never commands it. The check now
reads the speed the program commands, posting::posted_rpm (0 for a
probe, the tool's own rpm for a cutter), the same answer the post uses.

Pinned by probe_spindle_range::{a_probe_program_passes_the_spindle_range_of_a_tormach,
a_probe_posts_no_speed_and_a_cutter_its_own,
a_cutter_below_the_minimum_is_still_refused_beside_a_probe}.

Fixes #565

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
